{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0042386","isObsolete":false,"name":"hemocyte differentiation","definition":{"text":"The process in which a relatively unspecialized cell acquires the characteristics of a mature hemocyte. Hemocytes are blood cells associated with a hemocoel (the cavity containing most of the major organs of the arthropod body) which are involved in defense and clotting of hemolymph, but not involved in transport of oxygen.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"CL","dbId":"0000387"},{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"9550723"}]},"synonyms":[{"name":"arthropod blood cell differentiation","type":"exact"}],"children":[{"id":"GO:0042688","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0035168","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0042387","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0045610","relation":"regulates"},{"id":"GO:0007516","relation":"part_of"},{"id":"GO:0035163","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0045611","relation":"negatively_regulates"},{"id":"GO:0045612","relation":"positively_regulates"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2015-12-09","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2010-12-17","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process in which a relatively unspecialized cell acquires the characteristics of a mature hemocyte. Hemocytes are blood cells associated with a hemocoel (the cavity containing most of the major organs of the arthropod body) which are involved in defense and clotting of hemolymph, but not involved in transport of oxygen."},{"timestamp":"2010-12-17","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process whereby a relatively unspecialized cell acquires the characteristics of a mature hemocyte. Hemocytes are blood cells associated with a hemocoel (the cavity containing most of the major organs of the arthropod body) which are involved in defense and clotting of hemolymph, but not involved in transport of oxygen."},{"timestamp":"2010-09-03","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0030097 (hemopoiesis)"},{"timestamp":"2010-0