{"timestamp":"2007-04-06","action":"Added","category":"SYNONYM","text":"hemocyte differentiation (sensu Arthropoda)"},{"timestamp":"2007-04-06","action":"Updated","category":"TERM","text":"hemocyte differentiation"},{"timestamp":"2007-01-18","action":"Updated","category":"TERM","text":"hemocyte differentiation (sensu Arthropoda)"},{"timestamp":"2007-01-15","action":"Updated","category":"TERM","text":"hemocyte differentiation (sensu the Arthropoda research community)"},{"timestamp":"2004-07-07","action":"Updated","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process whereby a relatively unspecialized cell acquires the characteristics of a mature hemocyte. Hemocytes are blood cells associated with a hemocoel (the cavity containing most of the major organs of the arthropod body) which are involved in defense and clotting of hemolymph, but not involved in transport of oxygen. As in, but not restricted to, arthropods (Arthropoda, ncbi_taxonomy_id:6656)."},{"timestamp":"2004-07-03","action":"Updated","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process whereby a relatively unspecialised cell aquires the characteristics of a mature hemocyte. Hemocytes are blood cells associated with a hemocoel (the cavity containing most of the major organs of the arthropod body) which are involved in defense and clotting of hemolymph, but not involved in transport of oxygen. As in, but not restricted to, arthropods (Arthropoda, ncbi_taxonomy_id:6656)."},{"timestamp":"2004-06-27","action":"Updated","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process whereby a relatively unspecialized cell acquires the characteristics of a mature hemocyte. Hemocytes are blood cells associated with a hemocoel (the cavity containing most of the major organs of the arthropod body) which are involved in defense and clotting of hemolymph, but not involved in transport of oxygen. As in, but not restricted to, arthropods (Arthropoda, ncbi_taxonomy_id:6656)."},{"timestamp":"2004-05-08","action":"Updated","category":"TERM","text":"hemocyte differentiation (sensu Arthropoda)"},{"timestamp":"2004-05-07","action":"Updated","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process whereby a relatively unspecialised cell aquires the characteristics of a mature hemocyte. Hemocytes are blood cells associated with a hemocoel (the cavity containing most of the major organs of the arthropod body) which are involved in defense and clotting of hemolymph, but not involved in transport of oxygen. As in, but not restricted to, arthropods (Arthropoda, ncbi_taxonomy_id:6656)."},{"timestamp":"2002-11-27","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The process whereby a hemopoietic stem cells acquires the characteristics of a mature hemocyte. Hemocytes are blood cells associated with a hemocoel (the cavity containing most of the major organs of the arthropod body) which are and involved in defense, and clotting of hemolymph, but not involved in transport of oxygen."},{"timestamp":"2002-07-23","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"hemocyte differentiation"}],"xRelations":[{"id":"CL:0000387","term":"hemocyte (sensu Arthropoda)","namespace":"CL","url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ontology-lookup/?termId=CL:0000387","relation":"results_in_acquisition_of_features_of"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0042386","ancestorName":"hemocyte differentiation","relationship":"only_in_taxon","taxId":"6656","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Arthropoda"}],"aspect":"biological_process","usage":"Unrestricted","blacklist":[{"goId":"GO:0042386","reason":"1 NOT-qualified manual annotation exists with evidence code ECO:0000318 from this reference: GO_REF:0000033","category":"NOT-qualified manual","entityType":"protein","entityId":"A7RTM4","taxonId":"45351","entityName":"A7RTM4_NEMVE","ancestorGoId":"GO:0030154"},{"goId":"GO:0042386","reason":"1 NOT-qualified manual annotation exists with evidence code ECO:0000318 from this reference: GO_REF:0000033","category":"NOT-qualified manual","entityType":"protein","entityId":"A7S6A4","taxonId":"45351","enti